    { "q": "Direction: In the question, three statements are given followed by two conclusions. Statements: All pens are boxes. Some boxes are red. No red is blue. Conclusions: I. Some pens are red. II. No blue is a box. Which follows?", "o": ["Only I", "Only II", "Both I and II", "Neither I nor II"], "a": 3, "x": "I does not follow (pens may be outside red). II does not follow (boxes may include blue outside red). Neither follows.", "s": "Reasoning Ability", "t": "Syllogism & inequality", "d": 3 },
    { "q": "Study the data: Company revenue ₹120 cr, expenses ₹90 cr. If next year revenue grows 15% and expenses grow 10%, the profit increases by:", "o": ["20%", "25%", "30%", "35%"], "a": 2, "x": "Profit now 30; next year revenue 138, expenses 99 → profit 39. Increase = 9/30 = 30%.", "s": "Data Analysis & Interpretation", "t": "Caselet & arithmetic DI", "d": 2 },
